After editing files:

1. Check what changed

                git status

2. Add changes (stage them)

               git add .

3. Save changes (commit)
               git commit -m "describe what you changed"

4. Upload to GitHub (push)
               git push origin main

5. Full cycle after coding
               git status
               git add .
               git commit -m "update code"
               git push origin main


6. On another PC (IMPORTANT)

     Before starting work on another computer:

                       git pull origin main
⚠️ Simple rule to remember
💻 After coding (send changes):
add → commit → push
🖥 Before coding (get latest):
pull
🔥 Real-life example
You changed code on PC A:
                        git add .
                        git commit -m "added new feature"
                        git push origin main
Now on PC B:
                        git pull origin main